        "title": "Zoonoses and One Health - The Human-Animal-Environment Interface",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "**Read left to right.** A zoonosis is a disease that moves from animals to humans. Most do not\nspread human-to-human and burn out (a \"dead-end\" infection like rabies in a person). The\ndangerous ones acquire human-to-human transmission and become epidemics. The whole argument\nfor One Health is that the cheapest place to stop the pipeline is on the left — at the animal\nreservoir — which is precisely where veterinary medicine operates."
    },
    {
      "id": "04-ZOONOSES-AND-ONE-HEALTH.md#003",
      "path": [
        "04-ZOONOSES-AND-ONE-HEALTH.md"
      ],
      "level": 0,
      "line": 1,
      "metadata": {
        "backsource_ids": "[proof-backfill:veterinary-medicine:04-zoonoses-and-one-health, git-history:veterinary-medicine:04-zoonoses-and-one-health]",
        "canonical_path": "veterinary-medicine/04-ZOONOSES-AND-ONE-HEALTH.md",
        "concepts": "[zoonoses, one health]",
        "current_path": "veterinary-medicine/04-ZOONOSES-AND-ONE-HEALTH.md",
        "id": "maxim:veterinary-medicine:zoonoses-and-one-health",
        "index_roles": "[guide]",
        "kind": "guide",
        "maxim_schema": "maxim.frontmatter.v1",
        "module": "veterinary-medicine",
        "remap_from": "[]",
        "remap_to": "[]",
        "root_concepts": "[zoonoses]",
        "section": "veterinary-medicine",
        "source_custody": "partial",
        "status": "source-custody",
        "title": "Zoonoses and One Health - The Human-Animal-Environment Interface",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "**Systems Bridge:** Spillover is a cross-tenant escape in a multi-tenant system. A pathogen\n\"sandboxed\" to one host species exploits a vulnerability (a shared receptor, a contact event)\nto execute on a new host. Most escapes fail to propagate (dead-end). The catastrophic ones\nachieve persistence (human-to-human transmission) and then it is a worm, not a single exploit.\nDefense is the same as in security: monitor the boundary (the animal-human interface), reduce\nattack surface (limit risky contact, wet markets, deforestation), and patch the reservoir\n(vaccinate animals) rather than waiting to treat every infected human."
    },
    {
