      "text": "### Rabies — the archetype"
    },
    {
      "id": "04-ZOONOSES-AND-ONE-HEALTH.md#018",
      "path": [
        "04-ZOONOSES-AND-ONE-HEALTH.md"
      ],
      "level": 0,
      "line": 1,
      "metadata": {
        "backsource_ids": "[proof-backfill:veterinary-medicine:04-zoonoses-and-one-health, git-history:veterinary-medicine:04-zoonoses-and-one-health]",
        "canonical_path": "veterinary-medicine/04-ZOONOSES-AND-ONE-HEALTH.md",
        "concepts": "[zoonoses, one health]",
        "current_path": "veterinary-medicine/04-ZOONOSES-AND-ONE-HEALTH.md",
        "id": "maxim:veterinary-medicine:zoonoses-and-one-health",
        "index_roles": "[guide]",
        "kind": "guide",
        "maxim_schema": "maxim.frontmatter.v1",
        "module": "veterinary-medicine",
        "remap_from": "[]",
        "remap_to": "[]",
        "root_concepts": "[zoonoses]",
        "section": "veterinary-medicine",
        "source_custody": "partial",
        "status": "source-custody",
        "title": "Zoonoses and One Health - The Human-Animal-Environment Interface",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "```\n+--------------------------------------------------------------------------+\n|                              RABIES                                      |\n|                                                                          |\n|   AGENT: Lyssavirus (rhabdovirus, bullet-shaped).                        |\n|   RESERVOIR: dogs (most human deaths globally), plus bats, raccoons,     |\n|              foxes, skunks depending on region.                          |\n|   ROUTE: bite -> virus travels up PERIPHERAL NERVES to the brain         |\n|          (retrograde axonal transport) -> fatal encephalitis.            |\n|   KEY FACTS:                                                             |\n|     * Once clinical signs appear, it is ~100% FATAL. Essentially no      |\n|       survivors. This makes prevention everything.                       |\n|     * Long, variable incubation (weeks to months) because the virus      |\n|       must travel the nerves -> there is a window for POST-EXPOSURE      |\n|       PROPHYLAXIS (wound care + vaccine + immunoglobulin) that           |\n|       prevents disease if given before symptoms.                         |\n|     * Vaccinating DOGS breaks the chain to humans. Mass dog              |\n|       vaccination has eliminated dog-mediated human rabies in many       |\n|       countries -- a textbook One Health win.                            |\n+--------------------------------------------------------------------------+\n```"
    },
    {
      "id": "04-ZOONOSES-AND-ONE-HEALTH.md#019",
      "path": [
        "04-ZOONOSES-AND-ONE-HEALTH.md"
      ],
      "level": 0,
      "line": 1,
      "metadata": {
        "backsource_ids": "[proof-backfill:veterinary-medicine:04-zoonoses-and-one-health, git-history:veterinary-medicine:04-zoonoses-and-one-health]",
        "canonical_path": "veterinary-medicine/04-ZOONOSES-AND-ONE-HEALTH.md",
        "concepts": "[zoonoses, one health]",
        "current_path": "veterinary-medicine/04-ZOONOSES-AND-ONE-HEALTH.md",
        "id": "maxim:veterinary-medicine:zoonoses-and-one-health",
        "index_roles": "[guide]",
        "kind": "guide",
        "maxim_schema": "maxim.frontmatter.v1",
        "module": "veterinary-medicine",
        "remap_from": "[]",
        "remap_to": "[]",
        "root_concepts": "[zoonoses]",
        "section": "veterinary-medicine",
        "source_custody": "partial",
        "status": "source-custody",
        "title": "Zoonoses and One Health - The Human-Animal-Environment Interface",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "Rabies is the canonical case: a ~100% fatal disease where the entire public-health strategy is\nto immunize the *animal* reservoir, not to treat the human. Vaccinate ~70% of the dog\npopulation and dog-mediated human rabies collapses. It is the cleanest demonstration that\nanimal health *is* human health."
    },
    {
      "id": "04-ZOONOSES-AND-ONE-HEALTH.md#020",
      "path": [
        "04-ZOONOSES-AND-ONE-HEALTH.md"
      ],
      "level": 0,
      "line": 1,
      "metadata": {
        "backsource_ids": "[proof-backfill:veterinary-medicine:04-zoonoses-and-one-health, git-history:veterinary-medicine:04-zoonoses-and-one-health]",
