      },
      "text": "### Influenza — the reassortment machine"
    },
    {
      "id": "04-ZOONOSES-AND-ONE-HEALTH.md#021",
      "path": [
        "04-ZOONOSES-AND-ONE-HEALTH.md"
      ],
      "level": 0,
      "line": 1,
      "metadata": {
        "backsource_ids": "[proof-backfill:veterinary-medicine:04-zoonoses-and-one-health, git-history:veterinary-medicine:04-zoonoses-and-one-health]",
        "canonical_path": "veterinary-medicine/04-ZOONOSES-AND-ONE-HEALTH.md",
        "concepts": "[zoonoses, one health]",
        "current_path": "veterinary-medicine/04-ZOONOSES-AND-ONE-HEALTH.md",
        "id": "maxim:veterinary-medicine:zoonoses-and-one-health",
        "index_roles": "[guide]",
        "kind": "guide",
        "maxim_schema": "maxim.frontmatter.v1",
        "module": "veterinary-medicine",
        "remap_from": "[]",
        "remap_to": "[]",
        "root_concepts": "[zoonoses]",
        "section": "veterinary-medicine",
        "source_custody": "partial",
        "status": "source-custody",
        "title": "Zoonoses and One Health - The Human-Animal-Environment Interface",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "Influenza A is the pandemic engine because its segmented genome can **reassort** when two\nstrains co-infect one host, swapping whole gene segments."
    },
    {
      "id": "04-ZOONOSES-AND-ONE-HEALTH.md#022",
      "path": [
        "04-ZOONOSES-AND-ONE-HEALTH.md"
      ],
      "level": 0,
      "line": 1,
      "metadata": {
        "backsource_ids": "[proof-backfill:veterinary-medicine:04-zoonoses-and-one-health, git-history:veterinary-medicine:04-zoonoses-and-one-health]",
        "canonical_path": "veterinary-medicine/04-ZOONOSES-AND-ONE-HEALTH.md",
        "concepts": "[zoonoses, one health]",
        "current_path": "veterinary-medicine/04-ZOONOSES-AND-ONE-HEALTH.md",
        "id": "maxim:veterinary-medicine:zoonoses-and-one-health",
        "index_roles": "[guide]",
        "kind": "guide",
        "maxim_schema": "maxim.frontmatter.v1",
        "module": "veterinary-medicine",
        "remap_from": "[]",
        "remap_to": "[]",
        "root_concepts": "[zoonoses]",
        "section": "veterinary-medicine",
        "source_custody": "partial",
        "status": "source-custody",
        "title": "Zoonoses and One Health - The Human-Animal-Environment Interface",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "```\n   WHY THE PIG IS THE \"MIXING VESSEL\"\n   ----------------------------------\n   Pig respiratory cells carry receptors for BOTH avian-type and\n   human-type influenza. A pig co-infected with a bird flu and a human\n   flu can let the two viruses swap genome segments (REASSORTMENT),\n   producing a brand-new strain with human transmissibility + novel\n   surface proteins humans have no immunity to. That is how some\n   pandemic strains arise."
    },
    {
      "id": "04-ZOONOSES-AND-ONE-HEALTH.md#023",
      "path": [
        "04-ZOONOSES-AND-ONE-HEALTH.md"
      ],
      "level": 0,
      "line": 1,
      "metadata": {
        "backsource_ids": "[proof-backfill:veterinary-medicine:04-zoonoses-and-one-health, git-history:veterinary-medicine:04-zoonoses-and-one-health]",
        "canonical_path": "veterinary-medicine/04-ZOONOSES-AND-ONE-HEALTH.md",
        "concepts": "[zoonoses, one health]",
        "current_path": "veterinary-medicine/04-ZOONOSES-AND-ONE-HEALTH.md",
        "id": "maxim:veterinary-medicine:zoonoses-and-one-health",
        "index_roles": "[guide]",
        "kind": "guide",
        "maxim_schema": "maxim.frontmatter.v1",
        "module": "veterinary-medicine",
        "remap_from": "[]",
        "remap_to": "[]",
        "root_concepts": "[zoonoses]",
        "section": "veterinary-medicine",
        "source_custody": "partial",
        "status": "source-custody",
        "title": "Zoonoses and One Health - The Human-Animal-Environment Interface",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "H5N1 (highly pathogenic avian influenza):\n     * Devastates poultry; spreads in wild birds globally.\n     * Spills into humans (and recently dairy cattle and other mammals),\n       with high case-fatality in the rare human cases.\n     * The pandemic fear: a few mutations or a reassortment that grants\n       efficient human-to-human spread. Hence intense surveillance of\n       birds and pigs. (This is WHY poultry outbreaks trigger culls.)\n```"
    },
    {
      "id": "04-ZOONOSES-AND-ONE-HEALTH.md#024",
      "path": [
        "04-ZOONOSES-AND-ONE-HEALTH.md"
      ],
      "level": 0,
      "line": 1,
      "metadata": {
        "backsource_ids": "[proof-backfill:veterinary-medicine:04-zoonoses-and-one-health, git-history:veterinary-medicine:04-zoonoses-and-one-health]",
        "canonical_path": "veterinary-medicine/04-ZOONOSES-AND-ONE-HEALTH.md",
        "concepts": "[zoonoses, one health]",
        "current_path": "veterinary-medicine/04-ZOONOSES-AND-ONE-HEALTH.md",
        "id": "maxim:veterinary-medicine:zoonoses-and-one-health",
        "index_roles": "[guide]",
        "kind": "guide",
        "maxim_schema": "maxim.frontmatter.v1",
        "module": "veterinary-medicine",
        "remap_from": "[]",
        "remap_to": "[]",
        "root_concepts": "[zoonoses]",
        "section": "veterinary-medicine",
        "source_custody": "partial",
        "status": "source-custody",
        "title": "Zoonoses and One Health - The Human-Animal-Environment Interface",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "The naming (H5N1, H1N1) refers to the surface proteins hemagglutinin (H) and neuraminidase\n(N) — the same proteins drugs and vaccines target (`virology/`,\n`medicine/02-ANTIVIRALS-VACCINES.md`). Surveillance of avian and swine influenza is one of the\nmost important standing One Health activities."
    },
    {
      "id": "04-ZOONOSES-AND-ONE-HEALTH.md#025",
      "path": [
        "04-ZOONOSES-AND-ONE-HEALTH.md"
      ],
      "level": 0,
      "line": 1,
      "metadata": {
        "backsource_ids": "[proof-backfill:veterinary-medicine:04-zoonoses-and-one-health, git-history:veterinary-medicine:04-zoonoses-and-one-health]",
