      },
      "text": "### Brucellosis — the slow occupational zoonosis"
    },
    {
      "id": "04-ZOONOSES-AND-ONE-HEALTH.md#026",
      "path": [
        "04-ZOONOSES-AND-ONE-HEALTH.md"
      ],
      "level": 0,
      "line": 1,
      "metadata": {
        "backsource_ids": "[proof-backfill:veterinary-medicine:04-zoonoses-and-one-health, git-history:veterinary-medicine:04-zoonoses-and-one-health]",
        "canonical_path": "veterinary-medicine/04-ZOONOSES-AND-ONE-HEALTH.md",
        "concepts": "[zoonoses, one health]",
        "current_path": "veterinary-medicine/04-ZOONOSES-AND-ONE-HEALTH.md",
        "id": "maxim:veterinary-medicine:zoonoses-and-one-health",
        "index_roles": "[guide]",
        "kind": "guide",
        "maxim_schema": "maxim.frontmatter.v1",
        "module": "veterinary-medicine",
        "remap_from": "[]",
        "remap_to": "[]",
        "root_concepts": "[zoonoses]",
        "section": "veterinary-medicine",
        "source_custody": "partial",
        "status": "source-custody",
        "title": "Zoonoses and One Health - The Human-Animal-Environment Interface",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "```\n   AGENT: Brucella (B. abortus cattle, B. melitensis goats/sheep, B. suis pigs).\n   ANIMAL DISEASE: late-term ABORTION storms, infertility.\n   HUMAN DISEASE: \"undulant fever\" -- recurring fevers, sweats, joint pain;\n                  chronic, debilitating, hard to clear.\n   ROUTE TO HUMANS: contact with birthing fluids/aborted tissue (farmers,\n                    vets, abattoir workers) and UNPASTEURIZED dairy.\n   CONTROL: test-and-slaughter programs + animal vaccination have eradicated\n            it from many national herds. A One Health success via the\n            ANIMAL side.\n```"
    },
    {
      "id": "04-ZOONOSES-AND-ONE-HEALTH.md#027",
