      },
      "text": "### Other major zoonoses worth holding"
    },
    {
      "id": "04-ZOONOSES-AND-ONE-HEALTH.md#028",
      "path": [
        "04-ZOONOSES-AND-ONE-HEALTH.md"
      ],
      "level": 0,
      "line": 1,
      "metadata": {
        "backsource_ids": "[proof-backfill:veterinary-medicine:04-zoonoses-and-one-health, git-history:veterinary-medicine:04-zoonoses-and-one-health]",
        "canonical_path": "veterinary-medicine/04-ZOONOSES-AND-ONE-HEALTH.md",
        "concepts": "[zoonoses, one health]",
        "current_path": "veterinary-medicine/04-ZOONOSES-AND-ONE-HEALTH.md",
        "id": "maxim:veterinary-medicine:zoonoses-and-one-health",
        "index_roles": "[guide]",
        "kind": "guide",
        "maxim_schema": "maxim.frontmatter.v1",
        "module": "veterinary-medicine",
        "remap_from": "[]",
        "remap_to": "[]",
        "root_concepts": "[zoonoses]",
        "section": "veterinary-medicine",
        "source_custody": "partial",
        "status": "source-custody",
        "title": "Zoonoses and One Health - The Human-Animal-Environment Interface",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "| Disease | Animal source | Human route | Note |\n|---------|---------------|-------------|------|\n| **Bovine TB** (M. bovis) | Cattle (badgers as wildlife reservoir in UK) | Raw milk, aerosol | Why milk is pasteurized |\n| **Leptospirosis** | Rodents, dogs, livestock | Urine-contaminated water | Flooding-associated outbreaks |\n| **Plague** (Yersinia pestis) | Rodents | Flea bite | Still endemic in some regions |\n| **Toxoplasmosis** | Cats (definitive host) | Oocysts in feces; undercooked meat | Fetal risk in pregnancy |\n| **Salmonella / Campylobacter** | Poultry, reptiles, eggs | Food-borne; reptile handling | Leading bacterial food-borne illness |\n| **Q fever** (Coxiella) | Sheep, goats, cattle | Aerosolized birthing fluids | Extremely infectious, environmentally tough |\n| **Hantavirus** | Rodents (deer mice) | Aerosolized droppings/urine | Severe pulmonary syndrome |\n| **Variant CJD** | Cattle (BSE prion) | Contaminated beef | The prion bridge (file 03) |"
    }
